# K03 NS-ROLES-2 (Codex K03-NS-ROLES-2-20261007-20; docs/LMX_semantics.en.md#resolved-head-consumption,
# #declaration-visibility): a named Structure's body takes the common roles of the root and a method.
# An unknown head in a named body defines a nested named Structure with its written content, as at the root: `b:
# zz` (zz retained), `c: 7` (a literal retained, no int is inferred), `d()` and `e: ()` (empty), `f:` with a block
# closed by its level (no end, no return).  Host runs; nothing of them runs at their definition.  Exit 7.
Host:
    int: n 0
    b: zz
    c: 7
    d()
    e: ()
    f:
        int: k 2
    n: 5
end: Host
fn: m () int
    Host()
    if: Host\n != 5
        return: 81
    if: Host\f\k != 2
        return: 82
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
